{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790264758,"nonce":"1f8QGMC82ONQvn7Bg7w0Ge9eKgI=","title":"Lua: a computed-key nil store leaves a constructor-born slot reading its old value","message":"A field every constructor writes with a non-nil value is typed without nil and read as always present, even when the shape takes a store under a computed key (the typer marks the shape dynamic-keys). The store clears the slot's present bit through the shape hooks, but the read ignores the bit. Same output on main dea6d08b and with the l2 field-read work, every tier; lua5.4 prints nil nil.\n\n    local a = {x = 1, y = 2}\n    local k = \"x\"\n    a[k] = nil\n    print(a.x, rawget(a, \"x\"))   -- zylua: 1 nil\n\nThe same through a helper (`local function clear(o, k) o[k] = nil end`) or a method (`function P:clear(k) self[k] = nil end`). A shape with dynamic keys should make its fields nilable (or not always present) in the lattice.","files":null}]}